{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-129109-r4522852","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Chili Cornbread Casserole","sourcePageId":129109,"sourceRevision":"4522852","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-11T22:15:05Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Chili%20Cornbread%20Casserole&oldid=4522852","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:35:27.604Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Inexpensive recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for casserole","Category:Recipes for chili","Category:Recipes for cornbread","Category:Recipes using bacon","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using chili powder","Category:Recipes using cooking spray","Category:Recipes using cornbread","Category:Recipes using cornmeal","Category:Recipes using cow milk","Category:Recipes using cumin","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using ground beef","Category:Recipes using instant coffee","Category:Recipes using jalapeño chile","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Texas recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"5387795f0bc3d1d12febffc46b4c0e67386a6266074c4d52d2676c2fa868a47f","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Casserole recipes|servings=6|time=Prep: ½ hour<br>Total: 45 minutes|difficulty=3\n}}{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Texas cuisine|Texas cuisine]]\n__NOTOC__\n==Ingredients==\n\n===Chili===\n* 4 strips [[Cookbook:Bacon|bacon]], cut in small pieces\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 1¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] [[Cookbook:Chili Powder|chili powder]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Coffee|instant coffee]]\n* 2 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] [[Cookbook:Jalapeño|jalapeños]] (canned)\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]]\n* 1½ teaspoons [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* 1 large [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], diced\n* 1¼ [[Cookbook:Pound|pounds]] hamburger meat\n* 1 pound [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]], cut into small pieces\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Black pepper]]\n* 1 can (15-[[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]]) diced [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n\n=== Cornbread ===\n* 2 tablespoons (¼ stick) butter\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Cornmeal|corn meal]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n=== Chili ===\n# [[Cookbook:Fry|Fry]] bacon at medium-high heat in big [[Cookbook:Skillet|skillet]].\n# Lower heat to medium and add the brown sugar, chili powder, coffee, cumin, jalapeños, oregano, and paprika.\n# Cook 3 minutes, stirring constantly.\n# Add onion and cook until soft, about 5 minutes, stirring frequently.\n# Add beef pieces and hamburger meat, and cook until lightly done (maybe 8 or 10 minutes).\n# While beef is cooking, start on cornbread.\n# Add tomatoes to skillet and cook 1 minute, stirring deeply to keep anything from sticking to the bottom.\n# Adjust seasoning as necessary, and remove from heat.\n\n===Cornbread===\n# Melt, then cool butter.\n# [[Cookbook:Whisk|Whisk]] butter, egg, and milk together.\n# Combine cornmeal, flour, and salt, then add baking powder and baking soda.\n# Stir liquid mixture into dry mixture.\n\n===Assembly===\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to [[Cookbook:Oven temperatures|425°F]].\n# Spray a 9x12-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] [[Cookbook:Pots and Pans|baking pan]] with [[Cookbook:Cooking Spray|cooking spray]].\n# Transfer the chili to the baking pan and smooth surface.\n# Spoon cornbread mixture over chili mixture, and smooth with a large spoon.\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] about 20 minutes, or until cornbread pulls away from the sides of the pan.\n# Serve in bowls, making sure every large spoonful has both textures.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* Beans in the chili would probably be too much starch.\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Texas recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for casserole]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes for chili]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bacon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chili powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using instant coffee]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornmeal]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cooking spray]]\n[[Category:Recipes for cornbread]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornbread]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using jalapeño chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cow milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Chili Cornbread Casserole","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 strips bacon, cut in small pieces","sourceText":"4 strips bacon, cut in small pieces","amountText":"4 strips bacon, cut in small pieces","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1½ ta